<!--
  RBCCM Platforms - Properties + Data
  ==============================================================
  Preset-driven 4-card grid of platform tiles. Each card = a
  DAM photo behind (source images carry the navy tone in pixels),
  with a title + body + gold "Explore" link. Whole card is an
  anchor. Fixed 4 slots; a slot hides when its TitleText is blank.

  Presets:
    strategy-and-economics-platforms
      Light-blue section, 4 navy-tinted tiles in a 1-col mobile /
      2-col tablet / 2-col desktop grid, per-card body max-width
      caps at 992+.

  Photo pickers (two per card)
  ==============================================================
  Two DAM pickers per card so editors can supply portrait-crop
  mobile vs. wide-crop desktop art. The desktop picker is used at
  >=992px and as the fallback <img> inside <picture>; the mobile
  picker is served at <992px via a <source media="(max-width: 991px)">.
  FocalPoint still applies to whichever image is visible at that
  breakpoint.

  Both Card{N}PhotoDesktop and Card{N}PhotoMobile are Type="Image"
  Datums backed by TeamSite's DAM picker. The nested <Image>
  skeleton with empty <Path/> and <Description/> is REQUIRED
  because a previous cross-component attempt hit "Datum ID=[...]
  Value is not a valid image" when the skeleton was omitted (see
  icon-carousel-properties.xml for the same note). Copy the
  skeleton verbatim for any new photo slot.

  XSL reads path + description off each Photo Datum and emits a
  <picture> element inside the card:
    Card{N}PhotoDesktop/Image/Path         becomes src on the fallback <img>
    Card{N}PhotoMobile/Image/Path          becomes srcset on the <source>
    Card{N}PhotoDesktop/Image/Description  becomes alt on the <img>
  Mobile Description is not read (decorative). When the desktop
  Description is blank the alt falls through to Card{N}TitleText,
  so the tile still has an accessible name.

  Focal point (optional per card)
  ==============================================================
  Each Card{N}FocalPoint is an optional String that overrides the
  CSS default object-position (50% 50%) for that card's photo.
  Values are standard CSS object-position ("50% 30%", "70% 40%",
  "top center", etc.). Leave blank to inherit the CSS default.

  Body max-width (optional per card)
  ==============================================================
  Each Card{N}BodyMaxWidth is an optional String (e.g. "274px")
  that caps the body copy width at desktop only. Kicks in at 992+
  via the CSS custom property rbccm-platforms-body-max-width
  (double-dash prefix at write time). Leave blank to inherit the
  CSS default of 340px.

  SEMANTIC TAG PICKER PATTERN
  ==============================================================
  Every editable text field ships as a pair:
    <Field>Text       String / Textarea with the copy itself
    <Field>Tag        Enum picker: h1..h6, p, div, span
  XSL emits the tag via xsl:element name="{tag}", guarded by the
  pickTag allow-list.

  CTA anchor tag is fixed at the whole-card <a> (semantic requirement
  for the entire tile being the link); only the visible CTA copy +
  href are Datums.
-->
<Properties ComponentID="rbccm-platforms">
</Properties>

<Data>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Last updated
       ============================================================
       Bump this timestamp every time you save content changes to
       this section. Format: YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM (24-hour clock).
       - Serves as a human record of when the section was last
         touched (visible at a glance to the next editor).
       - Also appended to the sidecar CSS + JS URLs as ?v={...}
         so browsers refetch the latest assets after a deploy.
       Example: 2026-09-12-1934  =  Sep 12 2026 at 7:34 PM
       ============================================================ -->
  <Datum ID="CacheVersion" Type="String" Name="Last updated (bump each time you save content - format: YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM, e.g. 2026-09-12-1934)">2026-09-12-1934</Datum>

